From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] dbusconfiguration: honour MissingIsAcceptable for fan inputs
Upstream-Status: Pending

For a "fan" class PID, each input is registered with the zone under a
paired name, fan sensor + pwm sensor (e.g. "FAN3Pwm_3"), so that one tach
can be tied to its PWM. MissingIsAcceptable, however, is resolved to bare
D-Bus sensor names ("FAN3"). spliceInputs() matches the two by exact
string, so a fan listed in MissingIsAcceptable never matched, and a fan
whose tach reads nothing still put the zone in failsafe:

  Zone 0 fans, entering failsafe mode, output pwm: 100
  Fail sensor: FAN3Pwm_3, reason: Sensor reading bad

When a fan's bare name is in the list, accept its paired name as well.

On the ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T, FAN3 cools only a passively cooled Tesla T4
and is driven open-loop from the GPU temperature: FANn tach feedback is
optional there, and the PID's feed-forward path (FFGainCoefficient 1.0)
already ignores the measured RPM when it is missing.

---
diff --git a/dbus/dbusconfiguration.cpp b/dbus/dbusconfiguration.cpp
index e7b0ddc9..7a69dc68 100644
--- a/dbus/dbusconfiguration.cpp
+++ b/dbus/dbusconfiguration.cpp
@@ -969,6 +969,19 @@ bool init(sdbusplus::bus_t& bus, boost::asio::steady_timer& timer,
                         pwmSensorName = getSensorNameFromPath(pwmPath);
                         std::string fanPwmIndex = fanSensorName + pwmSensorName;
                         archivedInputSensorNames.push_back(fanPwmIndex);
+                        // A fan input is known to the zone by its paired
+                        // name (fan + pwm), but MissingIsAcceptable lists
+                        // bare D-Bus sensor names, so the two never matched
+                        // and a fan listed there still forced failsafe.
+                        // Accept the paired name too.
+                        if (std::find(missingAcceptableSensorNames.begin(),
+                                      missingAcceptableSensorNames.end(),
+                                      fanSensorName) !=
+                            missingAcceptableSensorNames.end())
+                        {
+                            missingAcceptableSensorNames.push_back(
+                                fanPwmIndex);
+                        }
                         auto& fanConfig = sensorConfig[fanPwmIndex];
                         fanConfig.type = pidClass;
                         fanConfig.readPath = fanPath;
